        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Dal Lake, Srinagar, Jammu and Kashmir, Waterton Lake, southern Alberta, Canada, northern Montana, United States\n- Products: Shikara\n- Concepts: lake naming, mountain lakes\n\nFacts:\n- Dal is a lake in Srinagar, the summer capital of Jammu and Kashmir.\n- In Kashmiri, “Dal” means “lake,” so the name “Dal Lake” is a misnomer.\n- Waterton Lake is a mountain lake in southern Alberta, Canada, and northern Montana, United States.\n- The shikara is a type of wooden boat found on Dal Lake and other water bodies of Srinagar, Jammu and Kashmir, India.",
